      "text": "### Memory Pressure and Jetsam"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IOS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-IOS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:os:05-ios, git-history:os:05-ios]",
        "canonical_path": "os/05-IOS.md",
        "concepts": "[ios]",
        "current_path": "os/05-IOS.md",
        "id": "maxim:os:ios",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "os",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ios]",
        "section": "os",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "iOS Developer Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "iOS has no swap. Under memory pressure, the OS kills suspended apps silently (jetsam).\nYour app receives no signal when killed by jetsam — it just restarts next time.\nState restoration is how you recover from this gracefully."
    },
